Yes. I reviewed the two metadata datasets you have manually populated. I can see that you now have enough information to define the Periodic page before we write the SQL view.

I recommend keeping this page focused on cycle/schedule monitoring, rather than making it another copy of the Daily page.

1. What the Periodic page should answer

The main question should be:

“For each periodic DAG, when did it last run, when is it expected next, and what is its status for the current cycle?”

Main table

I suggest the detailed table contain approximately:

Column	Purpose
DAG Name	Job name
Master DAG	Parent workflow, if applicable
Source System	Source/application
DAG Type	DM / Extract / LRA / etc.
Frequency	Weekly / Monthly / Quarterly
Scheduling Type	MASTER / BRANCH / normal schedule
Schedule Description	Human-readable schedule
Expected Run Date	Current/next expected cycle date
Last Run Date	Most recent actual execution
Last Status	COMPLETED / FAILED / IN PROGRESS
Current Cycle Status	Expected/Completed/Waiting/Failed
Next Expected Run	Next cycle
Duration	Latest execution duration
Paused	Informational only

⸻

2. The most important field: Current Cycle Status

I would use a small set of business-friendly statuses:

COMPLETED

The expected run for the current cycle has completed successfully.

FAILED

The expected/current cycle has an execution and the latest/current run failed.

IN PROGRESS

The expected run has started but has not completed.

NOT STARTED

The current cycle is expected, but there is no execution yet.

WAITING FOR NEXT CYCLE

The previous expected cycle has completed and the next cycle has not arrived yet.

This last status is particularly useful for the Periodic page, as you previously agreed.

⸻

3. Example

For a monthly DAG running on the 2nd of every month:

DAG	Frequency	Expected Run	Last Run	Current Status
Job_A	Monthly	02-Aug	02-Aug	WAITING FOR NEXT CYCLE

On September 1:

Expected Run: 02-Sep
Last Run:     02-Aug
Status:       NOT STARTED

On September 2 after successful execution:

Expected Run: 02-Sep
Last Run:     02-Sep
Status:       COMPLETED

After that cycle is complete:

Status → WAITING FOR NEXT CYCLE

⸻

