One important boundary

I would not bring the Daily DAGs into this page just because their scheduling_type is MASTER.

The Periodic page should contain weekly/monthly/quarterly/other periodic workloads. The Daily page remains responsible for the daily workload.

If you’re happy with this high-level design, the next step should be to define exactly how expected_run_date and current_cycle_status will behave for each type:

1. Normal scheduled weekly/monthly DAG
2. Master-triggered periodic DAG
3. Branch-controlled DAG
4. DAG with multiple branches
5. A cycle that has already completed

Then we can write the Periodic view DDL cleanly without disturbing your working Daily view.
